    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d710a-45">

                <pb facs="0362" n="182" sameAs="frus:frus1945Berlinv02/pg182"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Truman Papers</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the President</hi><anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d710a-45-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Babelsberg</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-07-20">July 20 [1945.]</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Told Churchill about it.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d710a-45-f2"/> Also asked Churchill
                    not to let any proclamations be issued by control council while we are in
                    session here[.]</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d710a-45-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d710a-45-f1-content">
                <p>This brief memorandum is a manuscript notation by Truman on the Leahy memorandum
                    quoted in footnote 2, <hi rendition="#italic">infra</hi>. The conversation
                    referred to presumably took place either immediately before or immediately after
                    the Fourth Plenary Meeting, July 20.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d710a-45-f2" n="2" xml:id="d710a-45-f2-content">
                <p>The reference is to the subject matter of the following undated manuscript
                    memorandum by Leahy: “President inform Churchill. The French Government in an
                    adjustment of the exchange value of the franc is paying $17 per month to
                    American soldiers serving in France at the present time.”</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
